==Finnish==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|fi|fiu-fin-pro|*südän}}, From {{inh|fi|urj-pro|*śüδäme}}. Cognate with Estonian {{m|et|süda}} and Hungarian {{m|hu|szív}} and {{m|hu|szügy}} (chest of the horse).

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|lang=fi|[ˈsydæn]}}
* ''Note:'' usually pronounced with a long ''m'' in inflections and derivations (e.g., sydämen [ˈsydæmːen]).

===Noun===
{{fi-noun}}

# [[heart]]
# [[core]]
#: {{m|fi|reaktorisydän|reaktori'''sydän'''|nuclear reactor core, reactor core}}
# [[wick]] (of a candle)

